      "author_handle": "digestive.healing2",
      "author_followers": 1125,
      "caption": "Here are 10 simple ways to soothe acid reflux naturally:\n1. Drink Warm Water\nWarm water helps dilute stomach acid and supports digestion. Drinking a glass after meals may reduce reflux.\n2. Eat Smaller Meals\nLarge meals increase pressure in the stomach and push acid up. Eat small, frequent meals instead.\n3. Avoid Trigger Foods\nSome foods worsen acid reflux such as:\nSpicy foods\nFried or fatty foods\nChocolate\nCoffee\nSoda\nCitrus fruits\n4. Do Not Lie Down After Eating\nWait at least 2–3 hours before lying down or sleeping after a meal.\n5. Elevate Your Head While Sleeping\nUse extra pillows or raise the head of your bed to prevent acid from moving back into the throat.\n6. Drink Ginger Tea\nGinger can help calm the stomach and reduce acid irritation.\n7. Maintain a Healthy Weight\nExcess weight puts pressure on the stomach and increases acid reflux.\n8. Wear Loose Clothing\nTight belts or clothes around the waist can push acid up the esophagus.\n9. Avoid Smoking and Alcohol\nBoth can weaken the lower esophageal sphincter, making reflux worse.\n10. Chew Food Slowly\nEating slowly and chewing properly improves digestion and reduces acid reflux.\n✅ Important: If acid reflux happens frequently, it may be a sign of GERD or stomach ulcers, and a medical check-up is recommended.\n#kenyantiktokers #digestivehealth #nairobitiktokers🇰🇪🇰🇪 #fvpppppppppp #acid reflux ",
