      "author_handle": "doctorsood",
      "author_followers": 2700000,
      "caption": "Chronic throat clearing doesn’t directly cause esophageal cancer, but it can be a sign of silent acid reflux. When stomach acid repeatedly irritates the throat and esophagus, it can cause long-term inflammation and, if left untreated, increase the risk of Barrett’s esophagus, a precancerous condition. Managing reflux early helps protect your throat and esophagus.\nWays to manage acid reflux:\n🍽️ Eat smaller, more frequent meals\n🌶️ Avoid spicy, acidic, or fatty foods\n🕐 Wait at least 2–3 hours before lying down after eating\n🛏️ Elevate your head while sleeping\n⚖️ Maintain a healthy weight\n🚭 Avoid smoking and limit alcohol intake\n💊 Talk to your doctor about medications if symptoms persist\nHave you ever thought throat clearing could be linked to reflux like this?\nVC: @reecemandernutritionist\nFollow @doctorsoood to improve your health IQ and for similar content.\n#acidreflux #GERD #heartburn #reflux #medical",
